+# HARNESS_LOG — defect: dasha predictions show an error
+
+## Plan
+- Trace: components/dasha/DashaTimeline.tsx -> POST /api/dasha (app/api/dasha/route.ts) -> lib/claude.ts generateDashaPrediction.
+- Root cause: generateDashaPrediction still sends an assistant prefill message `{ role: "assistant", content: "{" }`
+  and prepends "{" to the reply. Newer Claude models (MODEL_PRIMARY = claude-sonnet-5) reject assistant prefill,
+  so the API call throws and the route returns 500 "Dasha prediction failed". The route comment already says
+  prefill is no longer used; prepareJsonString extracts the outermost JSON object on its own.
+- Fix: remove the prefill message and return block.text as-is (the system prompt already demands JSON-only).
+- Add a regression test under lib/ that mocks the Anthropic SDK and asserts no trailing assistant message is sent
+  and the returned text parses via prepareJsonString.
+- Run npx vitest run and npx tsc --noEmit.
+
+## Changes
+1. lib/claude.ts generateDashaPrediction: removed the `{ role: "assistant", content: "{" }` prefill and the
+   `"{" +` prepend; it now returns the model text as-is (still throws if the first block isn't text). I chose not
+   to use jsonReplyText, since it throws on max_tokens and would bypass the route's existing regex fallback for partial JSON.
+2. Added lib/claude-dasha-prefill.test.ts (mocks @anthropic-ai/sdk; asserts no assistant message is sent and the
+   reply parses via prepareJsonString).
+
+## Checks
+- `npx vitest run` -> Test Files 38 passed (38), Tests 281 passed (281) (includes the new test file)
+- `npx tsc --noEmit` -> no output, exit 0
+- Not run: I tried to run the new test against the pre-fix code (git stash), but that command was not approved.
+  I also did not make a live Anthropic API call, so the 400-on-prefill behaviour comes from the existing route
+  comment, not from something I observed.
